.TH KIWIX-CLI 1 "2026-08-25" "kiwix-cli 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kiwix-cli \- browse Kiwix libraries and articles from a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiwix-cli
[IOPTIONSR]
[ICOMMANDR]
.PP
.B kiwix-cli books
.PP
.B kiwix-cli search
\fB--book\fR IUUIDR [\fB--start\fR IN\fR] [\fB--limit\fR IN\fR] IQUERYR
.PP
.B kiwix-cli read
[B--widthR ICOLUMNSR] ILOCATORR
.PP
.B kiwix-cli home
\fB--content\fR ICONTENTR [\fB--width\fR ICOLUMNSR]
.PP
.B kiwix-cli random
\fB--content\fR ICONTENTR [\fB--width\fR ICOLUMNSR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiwix-cli
is a keyboard-first terminal reader for a Kiwix server. With no subcommand it starts an interactive Ratatui interface. The default server is the public Kiwix Browse service:
.PP
.EX
https://browse.library.kiwix.org/
.EE
.PP
Use a self-hosted server with \fB--server\fR or \fBKIWIX_URL\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --server " URL"
Kiwix server URL. Defaults to the public Browse service unless \fBKIWIX_URL\fR is set.
.TP
.BI --username " NAME"
HTTP Basic Auth username. May also be set with \fBKIWIX_USERNAME\fR.
.TP
.BI --timeout " SECONDS"
Request timeout from 1 to 300 seconds. The default is 30.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KIWIX_URL
Default server URL override.
.TP
.B KIWIX_USERNAME
HTTP Basic Auth username.
.TP
.B KIWIX_PASSWORD
HTTP Basic Auth password. It is intentionally not accepted as a command-line option.
.TP
.B KIWIX_CLI_DATA_DIR
Directory containing \\fBreading.json\\fR, which stores persistent history and favorites. The platform application data directory is used by default.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B books
List catalog UUIDs, content names, and titles for all available libraries.
.TP
.BI search " QUERY"
Search one library selected by its catalog UUID. Use \fB--start\fR for a zero-based offset and \fB--limit\fR for 1 to 50 results.
.TP
.BI read " LOCATOR"
Read a validated \fB/content/...\fR locator returned by search. \fB--width\fR overrides terminal-width rendering.
.TP
.BI home " --content CONTENT"
Open the home page of a content library. The Kiwix redirect is validated before the article is fetched.
.TP
.BI random " --content CONTENT"
Open a random article from a content library. The Kiwix redirect is validated before the article is fetched.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Start with no subcommand:
.PP
.EX
kiwix-cli
.EE
.PP
In the library list, \fBEnter\fR or \fBl\fR opens the selected library home page and \fB/\fR opens search. Article controls are:
.IP "j / k, arrows" 4
Move or scroll.
.IP "Space / b" 4
Page down / page up.
.IP "Tab / Shift-Tab" 4
Select the next or previous article link or image.
.IP "f" 4
Show Vimium-style hints over links and images in the current viewport. Type a displayed hint to open its target, use Backspace to correct input, or press Escape to cancel.
.IP "Enter / mouse click" 4
Open the selected internal link, external link, or image.
.IP "n / p" 4
Next or previous search result page.
.IP "g / G" 4
Beginning or end.
.IP "r" 4
Reload the current view.
.IP "R" 4
Open a random article from the current library.
.IP "H" 4
Open browsing history across all libraries on the current server.
.IP "B" 4
Open favorites across all libraries on the current server.
.IP "F" 4
Add or remove the current article from favorites.
.IP "d" 4
Delete the selected history or favorite entry.
.IP "h / q / Escape" 4
Go back. Press \fBq\fR in the library list to quit.
.IP "Ctrl-C" 4
Exit and restore the terminal.
.PP
Article HTML is rendered with styles for headings, emphasis, code, tables, links, and images. Internal Wiki links keep article history. Images are downloaded with the configured credentials before an external opener is launched. Small formula SVGs are rewritten as a larger vector SVG while retaining their paths and viewBox.
.PP
Successfully loaded articles are stored in persistent browsing history. History and favorites are unified across books, retain their source book and server, and only show entries belonging to the currently configured server.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
export KIWIX_URL=https://wiki.example.com
export KIWIX_USERNAME=wiki
export KIWIX_PASSWORD='secret'

kiwix-cli books
kiwix-cli home --content wikivoyage_en_all_maxi_2026-06
kiwix-cli search --book 12345678-1234-5678-1234-567812345678 'Rust ownership'
kiwix-cli read /content/rust_docs/A/Ownership --width 80
kiwix-cli random --content wikivoyage_en_all_maxi_2026-06
.EE
.SH SECURITY
Credentials are not embedded in URLs or passed to external openers. Automatic HTTP redirects are disabled. Home and random redirects must remain on the configured origin and inside the requested library. Unsafe schemes, traversal paths, malformed escapes, DTDs, and oversized responses are rejected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1/kiwix-cli.1
Recommended per-user installation path for this manual page.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/kiwix-cli.1
Typical system-wide installation path.
.SH INSTALLING THE MANUAL
.EX
install -Dm644 man/kiwix-cli.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/kiwix-cli.1
man kiwix-cli
.EE
